  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ritual music of the Jilala, Moroccan devotees of the saint ʿAbd al-Qadir al-Jilani of Baghdad, whose night ceremonies bring adepts into trance with an end-blown cane flute (gasba) over bendir frame drums and sung praise. Brion Gysin and Paul Bowles recorded a Jilala group for the 1965 Trance Records LP Jilala, and the Moroccan band Jil Jilala later took its name from the brotherhood.",
